WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.011
How they voted.

00:00:01.011 --> 00:00:07.102
Every vote you're about to see is from the official Hansard division record — the Parliament of Canada's own published record.

00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:12.193
Bill C-14 — the Medical Assistance in Dying Act of 2016.

00:00:12.193 --> 00:00:15.250
Third reading vote: one hundred and eighty-six Yea.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:16.670
Sixty-four Nay.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.806
Bill C-7 — the MAID Expansion Act of 2021.

00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:22.579
One hundred and eighty Yea.

00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:24.613
One hundred and forty-nine Nay.

00:00:24.613 --> 00:00:27.863
Bill C-11, the Online Streaming Act.

00:00:27.863 --> 00:00:30.999
Bill C-21, firearms restrictions.

00:00:30.999 --> 00:00:34.272
Bill C-63, the Online Harms Act.

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:39.126
These are the bills that reshaped Canadian civil liberties — and every vote is on the record.

00:00:39.126 --> 00:00:48.045
Forty-six currently sitting Members of Parliament voted in favour of both C-14 and C-7 — both aggressive expansions of state-administered death.

